{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/13/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/13`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/13/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：网格被分隔线划分为若干房间，每个房间内的彩色种子像素沿分隔线上的缺口\"生长\"到相邻房间，生长距离由种子所在房间内的同色像素数量决定。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black。\n  - 一种颜色（如 grey）构成正交分隔线网络，将网格划分为若干矩形房间。每条分隔线上恰好有一个 1 像素宽的缺口（缺口处为背景色）。\n  - 每个房间内有 0 到若干个前景色像素（称为\"种子\"），颜色各异，散布在房间内部（不与分隔线相邻）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对于每个房间中的每种种子颜色，数出该颜色在当前房间内的像素总数 N（N 范围为 1-5）。\n  - 找到当前房间的所有分隔线缺口。从每个缺口出发，向缺口通往的相邻房间内部延伸一条直线（方向为缺口的穿越方向：若缺口在水平分隔线上则向上或向下，若在垂直分隔线上则向左或向右），直线长度为 N 像素，颜色为该种子颜色。\n  - 若一个房间有多种种子颜色，每种颜色各自独立生长。若生长路径上有其他颜色的像素则停止生长（不覆盖）。\n  - 原始种子像素和分隔线保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要发现两层规则——第一层是数出每个房间中每种颜色的像素数量（视觉计数），第二层是理解这个数量决定了通过缺口向邻接房间延伸射线的长度，而非在本房间内发生变化。种子与生长效果分属不同房间，这一空间分离增加了规则的隐蔽性。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/271d71e2, train/6ca952ad, train/689c358e, train/d93c6891, eval/1ae2feb7, train/5623160b, eval/3e6067c3, eval/5961cc34\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"271d71e2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4268\nmechanism=0.5048\nlexical=0.0177\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:ray_loop, object:axis, object:marker, object:path, object:rectangle, operation:bfs_distance, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/271d71e2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/271d71e2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n\nRule:\n- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n\nKey insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"rectangular container with head that has same color as destination line\",\n  \"path\": \"head forward\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach the destination line or move_distance == s.inner_gey_pixels.num\",\n  \"type2\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src2\": \"inner grey pixels whose num == move_distance\",\n  \"transform\": \"change color to orange\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"grey pixels change color in order\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6ca952ad\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.4169\nmechanism=0.5212\nlexical=0.0126\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:hole, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6ca952ad.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6ca952ad.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected foreground objects with area greater than three pixels\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical downward ray in the object's original columns until its bbox bottom touches the grid bottom\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"translate the whole object once without changing shape or color\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear moved objects at their original positions; leave foreground objects of area at most three pixels fixed\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"689c358e\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3810\nmechanism=0.4969\nlexical=0.0156\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:axis, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:path, object:rectangle, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/689c358e.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/689c358e.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMark each arrow-like sprite's pointed frame endpoint with its color and the opposite endpoint black.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a one-pixel solid rectangular frame around a dominant interior background.\n- Inside the frame are monochrome six-pixel sprites shaped as asymmetric T arrows.\n- Each sprite has a length-4 bar and a length-3 crossbar one cell closer to the pointed end.\n\nRule:\n- For each sprite, follow its bar axis from the shorter end to the frame.\n- Paint that frame endpoint with the sprite color.\n- Paint the opposite endpoint on the same row or column black.\n- Leave the interior background, sprites, and all other frame pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The direction is encoded by the crossbar's off-center position: the nearer end is the pointing end.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"monochrome six-pixel asymmetric T sprites inside a solid frame\",\n  \"path\": \"orthogonal ray from each sprite's shorter bar end to the frame, plus the opposite ray on the same row or column\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint the pointed frame endpoint with the sprite color and the opposite frame endpoint black\",\n  \"transform\": \"leave the sprites, background, and other frame pixels unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d93c6891\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3614\nmechanism=0.4093\nlexical=0.0152\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:ray_loop, object:line_segment, object:rectangle, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d93c6891.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d93c6891.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove each gray bar into its adjacent orange rectangle as full stripes from the contacted edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The scene uses black outside space, yellow fill, gray one-cell-thick bars, and solid orange rectangles.\n- Each gray bar 4-touches exactly one orange rectangle; some orange rectangles have no touching gray bar.\n- Gray bars touching the same orange rectangle all have the same orientation.\n\nRule\n- Recolor every original gray cell to yellow.\n- For each orange rectangle touched by gray bars, count the gray cells assigned to that rectangle.\n- Horizontal gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange rows starting from the contacted top or bottom row.\n- Vertical gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange columns starting from the contacted left or right column.\n- Orange rectangles with no touching gray bar remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The gray pixels are not copied by shape; their count is transferred into the neighboring orange rectangle as edge-aligned row or column stripes.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"gray one-cell-thick bars s\",\n  \"dst\": \"4-adjacent solid orange rectangles d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s 4-touches d\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase s to yellow; in each matched d, repaint |matched s cells| orange cells gray as complete rows for horizontal bars or complete columns for vertical bars from the touched edge\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"1ae2feb7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3568\nmechanism=0.4625\nlexical=0.0117\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:ray_loop, object:axis, object:line_segment, object:path, operation:bfs_distance, operation:count, operation:draw_line, operation:ray_cast, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/1ae2feb7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/1ae2feb7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExtend row bars periodically across the opposite side of a separator column.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. A near-solid vertical separator divides the grid into two sides.\n- One side contains horizontal colored bars; the other side is blank target space.\n- Bars may be stacked by row and may sit at different distances from the separator.\n\nRule:\n- Identify the separator as the column whose non-bg cells are one color.\n- Treat the denser side as the bar side and collect each contiguous row run.\n- Process bars from nearest to farthest from the separator; for each bar, paint its\n  color every bar-length cells into the blank side without overwriting earlier paint.\n\nKey insight: Each bar's length is the period for its extension, and nearer bars claim target cells first.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Horizontal monochrome color bars to the left of a vertical separator bar extend rightward with periodic intervals equal to their pixel count.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"horizontal monochrome color bars left of the vertical separator bar s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"straight line from separator bar to the opposite grid edge, perpendicular to separator (rightward)\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint s.color at intervals where interval = s.pixel_count\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Process multiple bars by distance from separator: start with the bar closest to the separator, then proceed outward; do not overwrite previously painted colors\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"periodic pattern\",\n    \"interval spacing\",\n    \"ray casting\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
